=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015 + Phase-50 methodology:

ai_call_log table is empty when ai_mode='off'.
  The Audit decorator is the ONLY writer to the table. The decorator
  is in the chain regardless of mode (so we don't have to rebuild the
  Registry on every mode change), but the Provider chain itself is
  never invoked when ai_mode='off' — Settings flips Registry's
  active provider to nil/disabled at construction. No call → no
  decorator invocation → no row. The migration also documents this
  with a COMMENT ON TABLE referencing ADR-015 §I4. The frontend
  enforces the same shape: useAiUsage* hooks are still callable, but
  AiUsageCard returns null in off mode so no fetch is ever issued.

Audit is async + drop-oldest, never blocks.
  The decorator wraps Chat/Stream and returns the underlying result
  immediately. Audit rows go into a buffered channel; a goroutine
  drains them into the writer. When the channel is full we drop the
  OLDEST queued row (preserves recency, since incident triage cares
  about "what just happened") and bump the
  teslasync_ai_call_log_drop_total Prometheus counter. This means a
  slow Postgres can never starve Tesla telemetry or block a chat
  request — the worst case is missing audit rows, observable via
  the metric.

Cost calculator is data-driven and auditable.
  internal/ai/cost is a tiny package: a pricing table keyed by
  (provider, model) with rates expressed in micro-cents per 1M
  tokens. Local providers (ollama, mock) price at zero. Compute()
  clamps negatives to zero (defensive) and treats unknown models as
  zero with a note in the doc comment that operators see this
  immediately via the bug report → hash → digest pipeline. Tests
  cover every advertised model, the case-insensitive lookup
  contract, and the negative-token clamp.

Repo and handler are read-mostly.
  Today/ByFeature/Recent are all SELECT aggregates filtered by
  user_subject. ByFeature defaults to a 7-day window if no `since=`
  query param is passed; the handler also accepts a duration string
  (`since=24h`) for friendly URL construction. Recent is capped at
  AICallRecentMax=500 to bound page weight.

The shared UsageCard is presentational only.
  No hooks. No queries. Props in, JSX out. Both consumers (Tesla API
  and AI usage) derive their props in their own files — the visual
  contract lives in one place and is testable without mounting a
  query client. The DRY win is real because the original
  TeslaApiUsageCard had a 220-line JSX block exactly mirrored by
  what AiUsageCard would have needed.

aria-valuenow on the budget bar is intentionally unclamped.
  The original TeslaApiUsageCard exposed the raw pct in
  aria-valuenow (so a screen reader announces "250 percent" when the
  user is over budget) while clamping the visual bar width to 100%.
  We preserve both behaviours in the shared primitive — the existing
  TeslaApiUsageCard test pin asserts this and we kept it green.

=== CHANGES ===

Production:
  + migrations/000203_ai_call_log.up.sql
        TimescaleDB hypertable, 7d chunks, indexes on
        (user_subject, started_at DESC) and (feature_id,
        started_at DESC), compression segmented by user_subject
        with a 7-day compress policy and a 180-day retention
        policy. CHECK constraints on tokens >= 0, latency >= 0,
        cost >= 0. Composite PK includes started_at because
        TimescaleDB requires the time dim in any unique
        constraint.

  + migrations/000203_ai_call_log.down.sql
        Drops policies → indexes → table in reverse order so
        re-running the up migration on a previously-rolled-back
        environment is clean.

  + internal/ai/cost/cost.go
        Rate table for OpenAI (gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini, gpt-4-turbo,
        gpt-3.5-turbo), Anthropic (claude-3-5-sonnet-latest,
        claude-3-5-haiku-latest, claude-3-opus-latest), Ollama
        (any model → 0), Mock (any → 0). Rates expressed as
        micro-cents per 1,000,000 tokens (1¢ = 10,000 µ¢). Public
        helpers: Compute(), HasRate(), KnownProviders(),
        ModelsFor().

  + internal/ai/cost/cost_test.go
        Table-driven coverage of every model + the case-insensitive
        lookup contract + the negative-token clamp + the
        KnownProviders snapshot.

  + internal/ai/provider/audit.go
        WithAudit(writer) decorator. AuditRecord, AuditSink,
        AuditWriter interfaces. AsyncAuditWriter wraps an
        AuditSink with a buffered channel + drainer goroutine +
        teslasync_ai_call_log_drop_total prometheus counter
        (drop-oldest semantics on full buffer). Context helpers
        WithSubject/WithFeatureID/SubjectFromContext/FeatureIDFromContext.
        Stream relay computes token counts via len([]rune(Delta))
        because vendor counts aren't available mid-stream.
        request_hash = sha256(model || canonical-JSON(messages));
        redacted_digest = same as request_hash until F8 ships
        the prompt redaction layer.

  + internal/ai/provider/audit_test.go
        Tests for Chat happy/error paths, Stream rune-counting,
