=== AI-OFF CONTRACT ===

ADR-015 invariant evidence (only invariants this slice touches):

I1 (default-off):
  PASS — fresh DB defaults remain ai_mode='off' (no settings_repo
         change). The only schema additions are an EMPTY ai_call_log
         hypertable and the __usage__ registry entry; both stay
         empty/inactive in off mode.
  EVIDENCE: migrations/000203 creates the table empty; F0's
            ai_mode default of 'off' is unchanged; the audit
            decorator only writes when the chain is invoked, which
            requires the Provider Registry to expose an active
            provider, which only happens when ai_mode != 'off'.

I3 (baseline intact):
  PASS — Tesla API usage card visual contract preserved. The
         9-test TeslaApiUsageCard suite still passes including the
         budget-bar aria pin (875% over-budget value) and the
         camelCase-dedupe pin. No changes to Settings page,
         provider selection logic, or any non-AI page.
  EVIDENCE: vitest run TeslaApiUsageCard.test.tsx → 9/9 pass.
            UsageCard refactor is purely additive (extraction);
            git diff TeslaApiUsageCard.tsx shows only JSX block
            replaced by <UsageCard> wired with derived props.

I4 (zero egress in off mode):
  PASS — (a) Audit decorator is in the provider chain
            unconditionally, but the chain is only invoked when a
            provider call is made, and provider calls are only
            made when a feature is enabled, which requires
            ai_mode != 'off'. So no audit rows are written.
         (b) AiUsageCard returns null in off mode (settings
            undefined OR ai_mode === 'off') — no useAiUsage*
            hooks are mounted, so no /ai/usage/* fetch is ever
            issued. Verified by AiUsageCard test asserting
            requestMock was never called.
         (c) Server-side, mountAIUsageRoutes goes through
            usageGuardSettings which returns false for
            AIFeatureEnabled("__usage__") whenever AIMode == "off",
            yielding 404 from the guard layer.
  EVIDENCE: AiUsageCard test "off mode > renders nothing when
            settings are not loaded" asserts container has no
            [data-ai-feature] AND requestMock was never called;
            same for ai_mode='off'.

I5 (hidden UI):
  PASS — AiUsageCard emits the data-ai-feature="__usage__" marker
         only when the gate is open. The off-mode branch returns
         null with no DOM nodes whatsoever. The Playwright
         off-mode invariant walk picks up zero matches.
  EVIDENCE: AiUsageCard test asserts
            container.querySelector('[data-ai-feature]') === null
            in both off-mode branches.

I6 (404 routes preserved):
  PRESERVED — The three new /api/v1/ai/usage/* routes are
              registered through usageGuardSettings, which
              returns false from AIFeatureEnabled("__usage__")
              when ai_mode='off'. The standard guard.Wrap
              pipeline then returns 404 for those paths,
              matching the F0/F1 contract.
  EVIDENCE: aivet exit 0 ("OK — 5 AI route(s), 3 feature(s) in
            registry, TS mirror in sync"). The route count went
            from 2 (F0/F1/F2) to 5 (added 3 usage routes); the
            feature count went from 2 to 3 (added __usage__);
            both deltas are intentional and TS mirror is in
            sync.

I7 (per-feature opt-in; no silent restore):
  N/A — __usage__ is a server-side meta-feature with no per-feature
        toggle by design (D4.6). It is gated only on the global
        ai_mode flag. Users do not see __usage__ in the per-feature
        toggle list (it is excluded from AI_FEATURE_IDS via the
        SpecialCase flag), so there is no opt-in to opt out of.
        Mode-flip archive logic is unaffected because the archive
        only touches user-toggleable features.

I8 (no FK to ai_call_log):
  PASS — ai_call_log.user_subject is TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '' with
         NO foreign key. Audit rows survive a future subject
         deletion, satisfying ADR-015 §I8 ("audit logs MUST NOT be
         cascade-deleted").
  EVIDENCE: migrations/000203_ai_call_log.up.sql has no
            REFERENCES clause; user_subject is plain TEXT.

I9 (no PII in logs):
  PARTIAL (per slice scope) — ai_call_log captures token counts,
         cost, latency, model, provider, finish_reason, an
         opaque request_hash, and an opaque redacted_digest.
         Prompt content is NOT stored. The redacted_digest column
         is wired and populated (sha256 of the canonical
         message JSON), giving F8 the seam to plug a real
         redaction layer in without a schema change. Until F8
         ships, redacted_digest == request_hash; documented in
         the column comment.
  EVIDENCE: migrations/000203 column COMMENT on redacted_digest;
            audit.go AuditRecord struct has no message-content
            field; AuditWriter writes only the listed columns.

I10 (type system / aivet):
  PASS — aivet exit 0. 5 AI routes (2 from F0/F1, 3 added by F3);
